hose mysteries enveloped in human  experience as such so this here's where  he's going to tell us what some of these  mysteries actually are knowledge love  for example and revealed mysteries so  there won't be any confusion between the  things that are part of our existential  condition you might say and then  revealed mysteries such as the  Incarnation and the redemption he says  no effort of reason alone reflecting on  experience can enable us to attain to  these latter mysteries but reason alone  or there really is no such thing as  reason alone but the reason of the  concrete existing human being within the  situation's that they inhabit can  reflect upon mysteries such as that of  loving another person falling in love  falling out of love the mystery of evil  which he says is not actually the  problem of evil but rather a mystery the  mystery of the connection between the  body and the soul or the mind or  whatever it is the spirit whatever is  non-reducible simply to the body the  mystery of presence of participation  even a mystery of what constitutes  knowledge for Marcelle so all of these  are things that we can reflect upon and  they have their proper province within  philosophy particularly existential  philosophy that's not to say that they  can't be dealt with in many other ways  Marcel himself was a playwright and  approached things that he considers to  be mysteries through his dramatic  situations as we'll talk about now a  mystery is something for Marcel that is  distinct from but could fade into and to  generate back into what he calls a  problem and he thinks that much of our  current culture and the world that we  live in and the people that we are  is concerned primarily with problems  things that can be solved things that  are matters of desire and fear things  that we can formulate for ourselves  separate out and treat one by one or if  we like we're being ambitious treat in  multiple ways through what he calls  techniques things that could be the same  for you as they could be for me again  you know I've used the example  previously of YouTube tutorials those  are things that solve problems they  don't really raise mysteries unless we  start thinking about what is the nature  of my learning from another human being  whose image I'm seeing and yet maybe  dead or is located halfway around the  world or to take another example my  YouTube avatar if you look at the total  number of minutes viewed has at this  point lived more than twice as long as I  have out there in the ether what what is  that that's not a problem  that's more like what Marcel is calling  a mystery so let's let's see what he  actually has to say what he has to tell  us about these very important moral and  metaphysical enquiries situations ways  in which were rooted in being he tells  us that problems only go so far and we  can get past them  through an inquiry that is situated  beyond the problematical that goes  beyond it it doesn't mean that it's  there's somehow two realms that are  entirely separate from each other like  some sort of you know material realm  that we live in and then some ideal  realm or anything like that no they they  inter penetrate each other but it is  possible to go beyond the problematical  so he tells us that it is meta  problematical that is the the word that  he uses and we should talk about what  this meta actually means  here's an example of this he says I'm  inclined towards the affirmation of the  recognition of a participation that has  the reality of a subject this  participation cannot by definition be  the object of thought it could not  function as a solution but is rather  situated beyond the world of problems it  is meta problematical it goes beyond the  meta is much like the meta of  metaphysics this comes originally from  Aristotle and the books that we call the  metaphysics are meta tahu Sica they are  beyond the realm of the nature or things  that grow or the physical and they have  to do with being as such something that  undergirds underlies and yet penetrates  up into the merely physical right that's  the way a meta problematical thing  becomes a mystery it's not meta in the  way that other people might talk about  it for example when we think about meta  language right when we say we're doing a  metalinguistic thing we're using  language about language and generally  when we're doing philosophy of language  or linguistics the meta linguistic is  understood is sort of you know  referential above the other language it  governs it it tells it what to do we can  understand this sort of algorithmically  that's understanding it in a  problematical way still so meta  problematical he tells us a couple  different formulations of mystery all of  which are a little bit metaphorical but  can give us a good sense of it a mystery  he says is a problem that encroaches on  its own data what does that mean that  means that there's a certain self  referentiality and you might even say a  certain subjectivity there how does that  happen well problems exist for us  but they can be separated out from us  mysteries include us  they involve us they entangle us and  sooner or later were the one sort of  providing the driving engine the problem  can actually be applied to itself  you see Plato dealing with things like  this and asking questions rather  innocuously like well is justice itself  just that's not a problem that's more of  a what Marcel is calling a mystery a  problem that encroaches on its own data  he also tells us that there's a little  bit later a mystery involves reflection  reflecting on reflection or what Marcel  likes to call second reflection when  we're engaged in the world of problems  we are doing reflection we are thinking  about things say that last year and in  French means to think about to ponder to  consider right and so I might consider a  technical problem like how do I make  this book look as if I haven't been  setting it down in the way that it is or  where should I put the bookmarks in this  book right or how do I tie this tie I  can think about those things I can also  think about is this a proper time for me  to be wearing a tie what do I want to  convey to you the viewer that might be  something that's a problem as well but  it might start to extend into the realm  of mystery why should I be wearing a  time what is it connote ik is it because  I'm wearing as some people have called  it the part of the uniform of the  bourgeoisie no is it just because I love  wearing ties no it's because I want to  convey a certain sort of seriousness or  taking something as being important I've  done this with my students since I began  teaching and I was not a person who wore  tights much before that  nor am i a person who wears ties much  outside of this context or in business  and now notice I'm involved in this  question it's not purely subjective  though your understanding it you're  hearing it there's a connection possible  for you it can turn just into a problem  for you how do I understand dr. Sadler  or let me get him past his tie  predicament or something like that but  it also offers the possibility for some  sort of dialogue some sort of genuine  communication some sort of sharing some  sort of participation over you know  rather trivial example that can mean  much much more we're involved whether we  realize it or not in opportunities to  explore mysteries all of the time that  sometimes more than others and weddings  at funerals at births at you know  getting an award losing an award  consoling a friend who has had a  terrible breakup applying for a job all  of these things are within the realm of  the problematical at first but then can  be part of the mystery right and that  involves reflection on reflection  thinking about what you what you're  thinking and how other people think  about it and then thinking about that  some more it doesn't mean to lose  yourself entirely in abstraction in a  way this provides a possibility for  things to be even more concrete he also  tells us another formulation that a  problem or a mystery is a problem is a  wonderful phrase that trespasses on its  own givenness or data and I like that  that term trespasses because it implies  a certain sense of you know going beyond  what the rules are allowing but the  rules don't don't matter so much here so  what then is this beyond what is the  mysterious Marcel thinks that it's  inevitably going to be  it involves us within the problem as  those for whom the problem exists we  become conscious of ourselves not just  as problem solvers but as those who in  some way contribute to how the problem  is formulated or how the problem is  being looked at or whether we even need  to go beyond it and view it no longer  just as a problem but perhaps as an  opportunity as a dialogue as an exchange  as a mystery he also thinks that  mysteries are dramatic they're not  purely personal in the sense of being  intensely you know involving one subject  for whom you know they carry this  terrible burden by themselves know most  of these arise within a life that we  share together not necessarily a life  that we understand entirely either on  our own or with each other we don't  always have the same viewpoints on it  the same perspectives but we are within  dramatic situations as you might say  characters are in a play Marcel was a  great playwright so you understood that  it also involves us with something  beyond ourselves and it may be something  greater than ourselves  quite often the key to understanding  something fully is a mystery is a sense  of humility about our own part and how  much we matter in relation to something  greater he tells us that that we are  involved in how we grasp this and  there's a lot of scope for how personal  development or choices or the habits  that we develop would play a role in  this and he discusses that at different  points in this for example do we feel  hope or despair that's not a simple  choice that we turn on or off but it  does involve our being and our choices  and our relations to  other things out there and despairing  may make it impossible for us to grasp  certain mysteries that hope could open  up to us he goes on and he tells us that  mysteries are as he says real there's a  really great discussion here  he says the meta problematical some  people might say is just a content of  thought why not inquire about its mode  of existence as such what assures us of  his existence how do we know that any of  this stuff really exists is this not  itself problematical to the highest  degree he says my response to this is as  categorical as can be to think the meta  problematic is to affirm it as  indubitably real to think it is to  affirm it there is no thinking it and  denying it at the same time and to  affirm it as being indubitably real that  is it cannot be doubted this is sort of  like the Cartesian coach ito he tells us  something I cannot doubt without  contradiction something that doubt  doesn't really make sense and he says we  are in a zone where it's impossible to  dissociate the idea itself from the  degree of certitude that it carries this  idea is certitude it is its own  assurance and to that extent is  something other and more than an idea  now this is not to say that mystery has  suddenly become you know transparent and  and you know they they present  themselves with perfect certainty to us  like for example the mystery of evil but  we know that the mystery exists we know  that we're dealing with something that  matters that is real that isn't just in  our heads or in social discourse or a  figment of you know some persons  imagination that's been transferred to  us in some way we're dealing with  something that has reality you could say  in itself if that wasn't a little bit  misleading  in itself in such a way as it can reach  to us and we can proceed into it might  be another way of saying it now there is  a one more thing to discuss in  clarifying this notion of mystery and  that is a temptation Marcelle says that  there is not a clear dividing line with  mystery on one side and problem on the  other and we can just say Oh leave those  problems behind go them over here to the  mysteries this is where the real action  is or anything like that that would be  nonsense in part because we do in fact  have a world of legitimate problems that  we do have to address not everything has  to be a mystery but if there are  mysteries then we want to be able to  acknowledge them as such and it's a  struggle sometimes to be able to do so  especially for people who are used to  thinking everything of everything in  terms of problems to be solved for  whatever reason however they managed to  get into that situation even for those  of us who are willing to say yes there  there are mysteries there's still a  temptation to reduce mysteries to  problems why because problems are more  tractable they're more manageable  they are solvable we might be able to  come up with some sort of technique for  addressing them and so there's a  constant temptation that we have to  struggle against to reduce mysteries or  degenerate mysteries to problems he  tells us that one thing that we can see  is that a mystery placed before  reflection he says tends inevitably to  degrade itself into a problem and he  gives us an example of that the mystery  which we easily see did you to generate  itself into the problem of evil  something to be solved by philosophers  through arguments another thing that he  does tell us  well is that the mystery of being in  some respect lies beyond knowledge he  says that to admit the meta  problematical is to acknowledge the  premise II of being over knowledge now  to being as affirmed but rather of being  affirming itself it is to recognize that  knowledge is enveloped by being that it  is in some manner interior to being he  says from this point of view as opposed  to what epistemology the study of  knowledge strives vainly to establish  there really is a mystery of knowledge  knowledge derives from a mode of  participation no theory of knowledge can  account for because the theory itself  presupposes this participation it's a  very common mistake in not only modern  philosophy but in many other fields to  begin from a demand that epistemology be  addressed before everything else and  that's a demand that everything be  treatable in terms of some sort of neat  tidy theoretical presentation or some  sort of technique and what that ignores  is the fact that even bringing up  knowledge itself is already a mystery  it's a mystery within being not the  reverse where knowledge would reveal to  us all the conditions of being so  hopefully this gives you some sense of  what Marcel means in speaking about a  mystery and how it differs from a  problem  you
 

